)!Scripting: Reframe common belief
ú487
’‰â€¢ CHALLENGE the implicit beliefs of your audience. This is what separates forgettable content from content that gets saved and shared.
ú488
­¤â€¢ If you show people that their current mental model is wrong or incomplete, you create a "wait, what?" moment, which makes the lesson stick. Here are the steps:
ú489
F>â€¢ State conventional wisdom: "Most people think you need x"
ú490
?7â€¢ Introduce flaw: "But that's not true because of y"
ú491
%â€¢ Briefly give explanation
ú492
h`â€¢ This works because it creates cognitive tension and positions you as someone with authority
